Is there a plan to add MCTPNetworkId in future?

Hi Ed,
For YV4, we plan to use this schema since NICs 0–3 are statically mapped to EID 90–93. We can keep the same schema for static assignments as you mentioned.

Here’s an example of the "platform" level configuration integrated into the board JSON:
diff --git a/configurations/meta/yosemite4_spiderboard_adc_ti_pwr_ti.json b/configurations/meta/yosemite4_spiderboard_adc_ti_pwr_ti.json
index 1a91a07..4523036 100644
--- a/configurations/meta/yosemite4_spiderboard_adc_ti_pwr_ti.json
+++ b/configurations/meta/yosemite4_spiderboard_adc_ti_pwr_ti.json
@@ -1163,6 +1163,40 @@
                 }
             ],
             "Type": "TMP75"
+        },
+        {
+            "Type": "NIC",
+            "Name": "NIC_1",
+            "NCSITransportType": "MCTP",
+            "NCSITransportInfo": {
+                "MCTPEndpointId": 90,
+                "MCTPNetworkId": 1
+            }
+        },
+        {
+            "Type": "NIC",
+            "Name": "NIC_2",
+            "NCSITransportType": "RBT",
+            "NCSITransportInfo": {
+                "InterfaceName": "eth0"
+            }
+        },
+        {
+            "Type": "NIC",
+            "Name": "NIC_3",
+            "NCSITransportType": "RBT",
+            "NCSITransportInfo": {
+                "InterfaceName": "eth1"
+            }
+        },
+        {
+            "Type": "NIC",
+            "Name": "NIC_4",
+            "NCSITransportType": "MCTP",
+            "NCSITransportInfo": {
+                "MCTPEndpointId": 93,
+                "MCTPNetworkId": 1
+            }
         }
     ],
     "Name": "Yosemite 4 Spider Board",

Below is the static assignment configuration for YV4:
https://github.com/openbmc/openbmc/blob/master/meta-facebook/meta-yosemite4/recipes-phosphor/gpio/phosphor-gpio-monitor/configure-nic-mctp-endpoint

Let me know if you have any further questions, ty.
